  [1mOne step left on your side:[0m save the staging CA to [38;5;153mstaging-ca.pem[39m at the repo root. Until that file exists,
  [38;5;153msync_staging.py[39m fails with [38;5;153mCould not find a suitable TLS CA certificate bundle, invalid path: .../staging-ca.pem[39m —
  loud, not silent. You can grab it with:

  openssl s_client -showcerts -connect reports.staging.example:443 </dev/null 2>/dev/null \
    | openssl x509 -outform PEM > staging-ca.pem

  Verify the fingerprint out-of-band before trusting it — pulling the cert over the same connection you're trying to
  authenticate only helps against passive interception.

